  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}\u20610) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
